: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://romanlutz.github.io&quot;&gt;https://romanlutz.github.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none; margin-bottom: 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/linkedin.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;linkedin&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://linkedin.com/in/romanlutz&quot;&gt;in/romanlutz&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none; margin-bottom: 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/bluesky.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;bluesky&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://bsky.app/profile/romanlutz.bsky.social&quot;&gt;@romanlutz.bsky.social&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Popular Repository&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/romanlutz/NFLPlayPrediction&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NFLPlayPrediction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;38 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;11&lt;br&gt;Based on NFL game data, we want to predict the success of a play. This can be used to insert different strategies before the play is call…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Other Repositories (Pinned)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/microsoft/PyRIT&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PyRIT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;4.6k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;923&lt;br&gt;The Python Risk Identification Tool for generative AI (PyRIT) is an open source framework built to empower security professionals and engineers to proactively identify risks in generative AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/fairlearn/fairlearn&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;fairlearn&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;2.3k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;519&lt;br&gt;A Python package to assess and improve fairness of machine learning models.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/microsoft/responsible-ai-toolbox&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;responsible-ai-toolbox&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;1.8k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;501&lt;br&gt;Responsible AI Toolbox is a suite of tools providing model and data exploration and assessment user interfaces and libraries that enable a better understanding of AI systems. These interfaces and libraries empower developers and stakeholders of AI systems to develop and monitor AI more responsibly, and take better data-driven actions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/romanlutz/romanlutz.github.io&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;romanlutz.github.io&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;4 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Roman Lutz&amp;#39;s website&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
      
